#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# integer_reverse

#% text
# `integer_reverse(n)` gives the integer with the decimal digits of `n` in reverse order.

#% text
# `integer_reverse(n, b)` reverses the digits in base `b`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Leading zeros of the result are dropped: `integer_reverse(120)` is 21.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
integer_reverse(12345)
#% output
#= 54321

#% cell
integer_reverse(120)
#% output
#= 21

#% cell
integer_reverse(11, 2)
#% output
#= 13

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The palindromes among the squares below 1000:

#% cell
select(table(k^2, k, 31), s => integer_reverse(s) == s)
#% output
#= [1, 4, 9, 121, 484, 676]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_digits`, `from_digits`
